# 1006 - In-Game Text Editor via Rmail

## Status
- Created: 2026-04-05
- Phase: 3
- Priority: Medium
- Depends: 163 (Custom class Lua format - establishes rmail infrastructure)

## Overview

Use the WoW game client as a text editing interface through an AIO addon that embeds
nvim-style editing. Messages composed in-game are sent through rmail to recipients.
To non-recipients, the message appears as **static** - unintelligible noise. To the
intended recipient with the shared key, the message is crystal clear.

This creates a communication channel that bypasses the game entirely - you're talking
through the filesystem, not through WoW's chat system. NPCs, the server, other players -
none of them can tell what you're saying. Only your listener understands.

## Current Behavior
- Chat goes through WoW's built-in systems (say, whisper, guild, etc.)
- All chat is logged and visible to server operators
- No encrypted player-to-player communication
- No in-game text editing beyond the basic chat box

## Intended Behavior

### The Editor Interface
- AIO addon provides nvim-style text editing window
- Modal editing: normal mode, insert mode, visual mode
- Basic commands: i, a, o, dd, yy, p, :w, :q, :wq
- Frame appears over game world, can be toggled with keybind
- Supports multi-line editing for longer messages

### Message Composition Flow
```
1. Player opens editor (/editor or keybind)
2. Types recipient: :to alice
3. Types subject: :subject Meeting at Goldshire
4. Types message body in normal editing
5. Saves and sends: :wq
6. Message written to player's rmail outbox
7. rmail daemon syncs to recipient's inbox
8. Recipient sees notification in-game
```

### The Static Effect

When a message is transmitted, it manifests in-game as:
- NPC speech bubbles with garbled text
- Environmental text objects with corrupted characters
- Chat messages that appear as line noise: `▒░▓█▒▓░▒`

To the intended recipient:
- Same visual trigger, but text is readable
- Decryption happens client-side via AIO addon
- Only they have the shared key in their contacts file

To everyone else:
- Just noise
- Can't tell a message was even sent
- Plausible deniability - "I didn't say anything, that's just static"

### Technical Implementation

**Server-side (ALE)**:
```lua
-- Periodic check for outgoing messages from player's outbox
-- Path: /home/ritz/games/azerothcore-2026/game-mail/player-outboxes/<guid>/

function Rmail.checkPlayerOutbox(player)
    local guid = player:GetGUIDLow()
    local outboxPath = RMAIL_PLAYER_OUTBOXES .. "/" .. guid .. "/"

    -- Check for new files
    local files = scanDirectory(outboxPath)
    for _, file in ipairs(files) do
        if not file:match("^%.") then
            -- New message to send
            Rmail.queueOutgoing(guid, file)
        end
    end
end

-- When message arrives in player's inbox
function Rmail.onIncomingMessage(recipientGuid, senderName, subject, body)
    local player = GetPlayerByGUID(recipientGuid)
    if player then
        -- Send encrypted payload to client via AIO
        AIO.Msg():Add("Rmail", "incoming", {
            sender  = senderName,
            subject = subject,
            body    = body,  -- Already encrypted, client decrypts
        }):Send(player)

        -- Spawn "static" visual for everyone to see
        Rmail.spawnStaticVisual(player)
    end
end
```

**Client-side (AIO Addon)**:
```lua
-- editor.lua - nvim-style text editor

local EditorFrame = CreateFrame("Frame", "RmailEditor", UIParent)
EditorFrame:SetSize(600, 400)
EditorFrame:SetPoint("CENTER")
EditorFrame:Hide()

local mode = "normal"  -- normal, insert, visual
local buffer = {}      -- lines of text
local cursor = { line = 1, col = 1 }

-- Decrypt incoming message with local key
function Rmail.decryptMessage(encryptedBody, senderName)
    local contact = Rmail.contacts[senderName]
    if not contact or not contact.token then
        return nil  -- No key, can't decrypt
    end
    return Rmail.decrypt(encryptedBody, contact.token)
end

-- When static appears, check if we can decode it
function Rmail.onStaticReceived(payload)
    local decrypted = Rmail.decryptMessage(payload.body, payload.sender)
    if decrypted then
        -- Show readable message
        Rmail.showNotification(payload.sender, payload.subject, decrypted)
    else
        -- Can't decrypt - just see static (do nothing special)
    end
end
```

